type: software
title: "KherveTeX (kherveDOC): A WYSIWYG LaTeX document editor with Git-based version history"
authors:
  - family-names: "Kerhervé"
    given-names: "Gwilherm"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6449-1828"
    affiliation: "Department of Materials, Imperial College London"
version: "0.153"
date-released: "2026-07-10"
license: GPL-3.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/gkerherve/kherveDOC"
keywords:
  - LaTeX
  - WYSIWYG editor
  - document preparation
  - scientific writing
  - tectonic
  - version control
abstract: >-
  KherveTeX (kherveDOC) is an open-source WYSIWYG document editor that
  produces publication-quality PDFs via LaTeX. Documents are edited on a
  Word-style page surface backed by a typed document model, serialised to
  LaTeX and compiled live with the tectonic engine. It supports inline and
  display mathematics, figures, tables, citations, cross-references,
  footnotes, .docx and .tex import, and per-document Git version history
  with auto-commit and push.
